member.summary:
The triangle's edges from its first vertex, scaled by a power of two to unit size: the products of the angle and
circumcentre computations then neither underflow nor overflow, and an input scaled by 2^k gives the same values bit
for bit (review of M3: at 2^-500 the squared lengths underflowed and no triangle counted as bad)

does segment ab cross the open interior of pixel (kx, ky), exactly. A filter first ();
where it cannot decide, the exact test (). Refinement on the grid asks this for every
split point it tries (profiled: the BigInteger test was a tenth of the mesher's time on the Herne tiles at snap 0.01)

+1 if e lies inside the sphere through a, b, c, d (given positively oriented, Orient3d(a, b, c, d) > 0;
the sign is reversed for negative orientation), -1 outside, 0 if the five points are cospherical.
Exact (floating-point filter, integer arithmetic for the uncertain cases).

Simultaneously contract all groups by N rings. 
if bBackroundOnly=true, then non-background group borders stay connected,
otherwise they pull apart.

Basic implementation of marching cubes mesh generation, which can be applied to arbitrary Implicit function. Multi-threading enabled by default, so Implicit.Value() must be thread-safe (or set ParallelCompute = false).
Usage: set Implicit, Bounds, CubeSize and IsoValue, call Generate(), then read Mesh (a new DMesh3 each time). The field is treated as "inside" where it is below IsoValue, so a signed distance field (negative inside, eg from MeshSignedDistanceGrid wrapped in DenseGridTrilinearImplicit, or ImplicitSphere3d) gives a surface with outward-facing triangles. Vertices are shared between cells, so the result is closed if the surface does not leave Bounds. Bounds should extend at least one CubeSize beyond the surface. Cost is proportional to the number of cells, ie (size / CubeSize)^3. Example (remesh a signed distance grid): var iso = new DenseGridTrilinearImplicit(sdf); var mc = new MarchingCubes() { Implicit = iso, Bounds = iso.Bounds(), CubeSize = sdf.CellSize, IsoValue = 0 }; mc.Generate(); DMesh3 result = mc.Mesh;
[TODO] support locking on Implicit.Value()? May not be thread-safe!! [TODO] extension that tracks set of triangles in each cube, so we can do partial updates? [TODO] is hash table on vertex x/y/z the best idea? [TODO] hash table for edge vtx-indices instead, like old polygonizer? (how did we index edges?!?)

