var lscm = new LSCMParameterization(mesh);
ParameterizationResult r = lscm.Compute();
if (r.Succeeded) r.ApplyToMesh(mesh);   // r.Distortion.MeanConformal is close to 1

member.summary:
The symmetric n x n matrix from the entries of one triangle (an off-diagonal entry once, in either order;
entries given more than once are summed, so per-element assembly is fine), factorized at once: check
IsValid, then Solve().

ComputeStatistics skips triangles with area below DegenerateAreaFactor * diag^2 (diagonal of the bounds of
the triangles): their normals give no evidence. Relative, so the result does not depend on the model units;
1e-10 equals the absolute 1e-6 of geometry3Sharp 1.0.324 for a model of diagonal 100.

member.returns:
false if both inputs are empty, CellSize is NaN or infinite, the cell size is not positive or too small
for the octree, or the computation was cancelled, with Result null (also after an earlier success);
true otherwise (Result may be an empty mesh, eg an intersection with an empty input).

member.summary:
a check of each build's region, made as soon as the region is complete (null: none). If it fails, the build
does not copy the rest of the terrain (the composite is then not the whole terrain) and RegionFailed is set;
the overlap check and the rebuilds go on as without it, so the final build is the same

the slope faces as a TIN: vertices rounded to the nearest doubles, z the lowest incident plane there minus
'lower' (rounded to nearest from the exact value), faces triangulated at their exact corners; group id = piece;
z negated for fill
